+  // Keep loop fusions within a size budget. Without one, long chains such as
+  // the pad-accumulate adjoints of stencil codes grow into fusions with
+  // hundreds of operands and ~1000 fused instructions per output element: the
+  // elemental emitter then generates per-element code that neither vectorizes
+  // nor fits in registers, and such a fusion runs several times slower than
+  // materializing its inputs. This check is deliberately independent of
+  // may_duplicate(): the code-duplication check below is skipped when the pass
+  // runs with may_duplicate=false (multi-output fusion mode), which is exactly
+  // when the oversized fusions appeared.
